 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Congratulations on getting this far. Intermediate is definitely the longest level. Have you checked that our local language isn't causing you to stick It can be. Lots of people stop at that point. Have you tried songs, they're great for building confidence? Not if you enjoy it. Songbooks do get repeating, you're basically doing a season of school every year. The publishers should, but they don't always. Look for the red circle with a star as a clue it's wrong. That's the spirit. Keep a list of songs you want to learn, and watch teachers you like. You'll get there eventually, it's just a long path.",
